d = case['utility_threshold']\n    # Build maps\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {}\n    for n in nodes:\n        pid = n['parent']\n        if pid is None:\n            continue\n        children.setdefault(pid, []).append(n['id'])\n    # Find root\n    root_id = next(n['id'] for n in nodes if n['parent'] is None)\n    # Recursive traverse\n    def traverse(nid):\n        n = node_map[nid]\n        retain = not n['removable'] or n['utility'] >= threshold\n        if not retain:\n            return []\n        result = [nid]\n        for cid in children.get(nid, []):\n            result.extend(traverse(cid))\n        return result\n    order = traverse(root_id)\n    return {'retained_node_ids': order, 'visit_order': order}\n\nNote: The root is always retained because removable=False. But if root were removable? In fixtures, root is not removable.\n\nThat's it.\n\nNow produce the JSON with escaped Python source.\n\nWe need to be careful with newlines and quotes. The source code string must be valid JSON string.\n\nWe'll write:\n\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    threshold = case['utility_threshold']\\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        pid = n['parent']\\n        if pid is None:\\n            continue\\n        children.setdefault(pid, []).append(n['id'])\\n    root_id = next(n['id'] for n in nodes if n['parent'] is None)\\n    def traverse(nid):\\n        n = node_map[nid]\\n        retain = not n['removable'] or n['utility'] >= threshold\\n        if not retain:\\n            return []\\n        result = [nid]\\n        for cid in children.get(nid, []):\\n            result.extend(traverse(cid))\\n        return result\\n    order = traverse(root_id)\\n    return {'retained_node_ids': order, 'visit_order': order}\\n\"}\n\nWe must ensure that the string is properly escaped: backslashes, quotes, newlines. In JSON, newline becomes \\n, backsl